-- title:
--   RH height 14–100 — Bernstein certificate tables
-- statement:
--   The proposed power-coefficient, row-transformed, and bivariate Bernstein coefficient matrices for the 93 rational rectangles covering the 86 unit height slabs from 14 through 100. These finite integer tables are from sometik179’s certificate construction. Their polynomial identities, affine changes of variables, Bernstein transforms, positivity bounds, and rectangle coverage are verified by the main proof. This data module asserts no zero-location theorem and no numerical inequality.
--
--   **Port note.** This is a port, to the Mathlib `777aaa6` / Lean v4.29.0-rc3 environment of the Riemann Hypothesis mission tree, of the definition `TaoFivePrimes_RH14To100BernsteinData` (id `a0d3b86a-bb8b-4a98-9ffd-d725e586d95c`, env `0df444a`, published by @raresbuhai). The Lean source is unchanged.
-- source:
--   sometik179, height-14–100 Lean certificate proof, Prove2Me submission c9908072-d99a-4431-aad8-a72c6352619a (2026-10-03), https://prove2.me/submissions/c9908072-d99a-4431-aad8-a72c6352619a. Theta/Mellin foundations attributed there to Gabewhigham, accepted submission 7ab19408-190a-439f-81f8-63e983ebb00b. Ordinary-syntax literal data preserved from the recovered export.; ported from 0df444a definition a0d3b86a-bb8b-4a98-9ffd-d725e586d95c

